  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "Plain pages are always twisted",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Every plain planar page is twisted: a planar cubic bipartite graph has at least six square faces (Euler: the sum of 6 - |f| is 12) and at most five faces meet the junction square, so some square face lies among the page's own edges, where a Pfaffian signing needs an odd number of negations and the plain signing has none. Hence in a plain cubic Pfaffian brace every trisum square has three twisted branches (twists are inherited), and the polynomial mechanism of TWIST-COUNT A reaches no plain non-planar brace. Every 4-cycle of a brace is nice, so a plain non-2-colourable brace has no 4-cycle; with Robertson-Seymour-Thomas, the Heawood graph is the only cubic bipartite brace whose plain system is not 2-colourable: the Fano plane is the only non-2-colourable 3-regular 3-uniform hypergraph whose incidence graph is a brace.",
  "dependencies": [
    "TWIST-COUNT-20261030-001A",
    "THREEFOLD-GRAMMAR-20261030-001B"
  ],
